1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,412
Your app runs on a private port.

2
00:00:02,412 --> 00:00:04,385
The customer visits a public one.

3
00:00:04,385 --> 00:00:07,672
Something in the middle must carry each request across,

4
00:00:07,672 --> 00:00:09,225
and bring the answer back.

5
00:00:09,775 --> 00:00:14,063
That something is a reverse proxy, and today you build one with engine X.

6
00:00:14,613 --> 00:00:16,766
You will route one path to a backend,

7
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:18,977
see exactly what the backend receives,

8
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:21,013
and fix three things it gets wrong.

9
00:00:21,563 --> 00:00:23,483
Route it, pass the headers, prove it.

10
00:00:25,033 --> 00:00:28,105
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

11
00:00:28,655 --> 00:00:34,266
One: how a proxy works. One request in, one request out, and what gets lost on the way.

12
00:00:34,816 --> 00:00:36,051
Two: a live demo.

13
00:00:36,051 --> 00:00:37,722
Engine X serves a page,

14
00:00:37,722 --> 00:00:39,975
but the API path leads nowhere.

15
00:00:39,975 --> 00:00:41,792
We see the failure first.

16
00:00:42,342 --> 00:00:43,918
Three: we add proxy pass,

17
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:45,431
and the backend answers.

18
00:00:45,431 --> 00:00:48,394
Then we look at what the backend actually sees,

19
00:00:48,394 --> 00:00:49,403
and it is wrong.

20
00:00:49,953 --> 00:00:51,677
Four: we add proxy headers,

21
00:00:51,677 --> 00:00:53,976
so the backend learns the real host,

22
00:00:53,976 --> 00:00:54,997
the real client,

23
00:00:54,997 --> 00:00:56,402
and the real protocol.

24
00:00:56,402 --> 00:00:57,360
Then your turn,

25
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:59,084
with a lab that judges you.

26
00:00:59,634 --> 00:01:02,407
This is lesson two of the web servers domain.

27
00:01:02,407 --> 00:01:04,071
Last time you served files.

28
00:01:04,071 --> 00:01:05,735
Today you forward requests.

29
00:01:06,285 --> 00:01:07,544
Route, pass, prove.

30
00:01:09,594 --> 00:01:12,175
One request, two hops. Let us follow it.

31
00:01:12,725 --> 00:01:16,356
The customer asks engine X for slash API slash hello.

32
00:01:16,356 --> 00:01:18,205
Engine X is the front door.

33
00:01:18,205 --> 00:01:21,493
It is the only thing the customer ever talks to.

34
00:01:22,043 --> 00:01:23,564
Engine X opens a second,

35
00:01:23,564 --> 00:01:25,655
brand new request to the backend,

36
00:01:25,655 --> 00:01:26,795
on a private port,

37
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:28,379
and waits for the answer.

38
00:01:28,929 --> 00:01:30,134
Here is the catch.

39
00:01:30,134 --> 00:01:31,138
To the backend,

40
00:01:31,138 --> 00:01:33,681
every request now comes from engine X.

41
00:01:33,681 --> 00:01:35,153
Not from the customer.

42
00:01:35,153 --> 00:01:38,231
So by default the backend sees the wrong host,

43
00:01:38,231 --> 00:01:40,172
and the wrong client address.

44
00:01:40,722 --> 00:01:42,110
The fix is headers.

45
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:42,475
Host,

46
00:01:42,475 --> 00:01:43,279
X real I P,

47
00:01:43,279 --> 00:01:44,448
X forwarded for,

48
00:01:44,448 --> 00:01:46,055
and X forwarded proto.

49
00:01:46,055 --> 00:01:50,877
Four small lines that carry the customer's details across the hop.

50
00:01:52,427 --> 00:01:57,440
Go to the lab folder.

51
00:01:58,990 --> 00:02:00,889
Look around. Type: L S.

52
00:02:01,439 --> 00:02:02,402
A site folder,

53
00:02:02,402 --> 00:02:03,158
the config,

54
00:02:03,158 --> 00:02:04,120
a logs folder,

55
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,495
and backend dot P Y.

56
00:02:05,495 --> 00:02:07,214
That is our tiny backend.

57
00:02:07,214 --> 00:02:08,727
It is already running,

58
00:02:08,727 --> 00:02:10,789
on port eighty-one ninety-two,

59
00:02:10,789 --> 00:02:12,990
and engine X is already running,

60
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:14,708
on eighty-one ninety-one.

61
00:02:15,258 --> 00:02:18,906
Read the config.

62
00:02:19,456 --> 00:02:21,102
Look at the server block.

63
00:02:21,102 --> 00:02:23,209
Listen on eighty-one ninety-one,

64
00:02:23,209 --> 00:02:24,395
and a root folder.

65
00:02:24,395 --> 00:02:26,765
Then a location block for slash API,

66
00:02:26,765 --> 00:02:27,160
slash.

67
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,214
And it is empty.

68
00:02:28,214 --> 00:02:30,123
That is the gap we will fill.

69
00:02:30,673 --> 00:02:36,412
Ask for the home page.

70
00:02:36,962 --> 00:02:39,735
Welcome to CloudCart. Static files work.

71
00:02:40,285 --> 00:02:49,416
Ask for the API.

72
00:02:49,966 --> 00:02:50,888
Four oh four.

73
00:02:50,888 --> 00:02:53,582
Engine X has a location for slash API,

74
00:02:53,582 --> 00:02:54,930
but no instruction,

75
00:02:54,930 --> 00:02:56,561
so it looks for a file,

76
00:02:56,561 --> 00:02:57,624
and finds none.

77
00:02:58,174 --> 00:03:07,134
Ask the backend directly.

78
00:03:07,684 --> 00:03:07,954
Yes.

79
00:03:07,954 --> 00:03:09,235
Backend says hello.

80
00:03:09,235 --> 00:03:11,460
Notice the host line: local host,

81
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:13,348
colon eighty-one ninety-two.

82
00:03:13,348 --> 00:03:16,113
That is what a direct visitor looks like.

83
00:03:16,113 --> 00:03:16,922
Remember it.

84
00:03:17,472 --> 00:03:21,226
Open the config in vim.

85
00:03:21,776 --> 00:03:22,996
Go to line sixteen,

86
00:03:22,996 --> 00:03:24,215
the location block,

87
00:03:24,215 --> 00:03:26,718
and add one line inside it: proxy pass,

88
00:03:26,718 --> 00:03:28,195
to the backend address.

89
00:03:28,195 --> 00:03:30,698
Proxy pass is the whole trick: it says,

90
00:03:30,698 --> 00:03:33,650
send this location's requests to that address.

91
00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:35,511
End the address with a slash.

92
00:03:35,511 --> 00:03:36,474
That is a rule,

93
00:03:36,474 --> 00:03:38,464
not decoration: with the slash,

94
00:03:38,464 --> 00:03:40,774
engine X removes the matched prefix,

95
00:03:40,774 --> 00:03:41,416
slash API,

96
00:03:41,416 --> 00:03:42,571
before forwarding.

97
00:03:42,571 --> 00:03:44,304
We will see it in a moment.

98
00:03:46,354 --> 00:03:53,842
Test, then reload.

99
00:03:54,392 --> 00:03:57,379
Syntax ok, and reloaded, with no downtime.

100
00:03:57,929 --> 00:04:05,588
Ask the API again.

101
00:04:06,138 --> 00:04:07,386
Backend says hello.

102
00:04:07,386 --> 00:04:08,437
The route works.

103
00:04:08,437 --> 00:04:10,736
Now read what the backend received.

104
00:04:10,736 --> 00:04:12,313
The path is slash hello,

105
00:04:12,313 --> 00:04:13,232
not slash API,

106
00:04:13,232 --> 00:04:14,021
slash hello.

107
00:04:14,021 --> 00:04:17,502
That trailing slash on proxy pass removed the prefix.

108
00:04:17,502 --> 00:04:18,225
Without it,

109
00:04:18,225 --> 00:04:21,050
the backend would have seen the whole path.

110
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,313
But look at the host line: one two seven,

111
00:04:24,313 --> 00:04:24,908
dot zero,

112
00:04:24,908 --> 00:04:25,504
dot zero,

113
00:04:25,504 --> 00:04:26,033
dot one,

114
00:04:26,033 --> 00:04:27,886
colon eighty-one ninety-two.

115
00:04:27,886 --> 00:04:29,739
That is the proxy's address,

116
00:04:29,739 --> 00:04:30,996
not the customer's.

117
00:04:30,996 --> 00:04:35,232
And the three other lines show a dash: nothing was passed along.

118
00:04:35,782 --> 00:04:39,856
Open the config again.

119
00:04:40,406 --> 00:04:42,510
Seventeen is our proxy pass line.

120
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:43,083
Below it,

121
00:04:43,083 --> 00:04:45,123
add four proxy set header lines.

122
00:04:45,123 --> 00:04:45,505
First,

123
00:04:45,505 --> 00:04:45,824
Host,

124
00:04:45,824 --> 00:04:48,756
with the original host name the customer used,

125
00:04:48,756 --> 00:04:51,242
so the backend can build correct links.

126
00:04:51,242 --> 00:04:51,688
Second,

127
00:04:51,688 --> 00:04:52,389
X real I P,

128
00:04:52,389 --> 00:04:54,429
with the customer's own address.

129
00:04:54,429 --> 00:04:54,811
Third,

130
00:04:54,811 --> 00:04:55,831
X forwarded for,

131
00:04:55,831 --> 00:04:59,591
a growing list of every address the request passed through.

132
00:04:59,591 --> 00:05:00,293
And fourth,

133
00:05:00,293 --> 00:05:01,440
X forwarded proto,

134
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,141
the scheme,

135
00:05:02,141 --> 00:05:03,479
H T T P or H T T P S.

136
00:05:03,479 --> 00:05:04,945
We type them carefully,

137
00:05:04,945 --> 00:05:05,774
one per line,

138
00:05:05,774 --> 00:05:06,348
and save.

139
00:05:18,398 --> 00:05:24,499
Test, then reload.

140
00:05:25,049 --> 00:05:26,286
Safe, and instant.

141
00:05:26,836 --> 00:05:33,940
Ask the API one more time.

142
00:05:34,490 --> 00:05:36,725
Now the backend sees everything.

143
00:05:36,725 --> 00:05:38,051
Host is local host,

144
00:05:38,051 --> 00:05:39,937
the name the customer used.

145
00:05:39,937 --> 00:05:41,263
The client address,

146
00:05:41,263 --> 00:05:42,730
the forwarding chain,

147
00:05:42,730 --> 00:05:43,917
and the protocol,

148
00:05:43,917 --> 00:05:44,475
H T T P.

149
00:05:44,475 --> 00:05:46,640
If the customer used H T T P S,

150
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:48,246
the backend would know,

151
00:05:48,246 --> 00:05:51,947
even though the hop behind engine X is plain H T T P.

152
00:05:51,947 --> 00:05:54,181
That is why this header matters.

153
00:05:54,731 --> 00:06:01,558
Every request is written down.

154
00:06:02,108 --> 00:06:02,708
Who asked,

155
00:06:02,708 --> 00:06:03,368
which path,

156
00:06:03,368 --> 00:06:04,569
and the answer code.

157
00:06:04,569 --> 00:06:05,289
Two hundred.

158
00:06:05,289 --> 00:06:06,550
The backend's answer,

159
00:06:06,550 --> 00:06:08,230
passed back to the customer.

160
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:11,148
Run the judge.

161
00:06:11,698 --> 00:06:12,506
Five checks,

162
00:06:12,506 --> 00:06:13,313
five passes.

163
00:06:13,313 --> 00:06:14,659
The config is valid,

164
00:06:14,659 --> 00:06:15,736
the API answers,

165
00:06:15,736 --> 00:06:16,947
the path is clean,

166
00:06:16,947 --> 00:06:18,966
and the backend sees the host,

167
00:06:18,966 --> 00:06:19,706
the client,

168
00:06:19,706 --> 00:06:20,850
and the protocol.

169
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:23,363
Clean up.

170
00:06:23,913 --> 00:06:27,518
Engine X stopped, the backend stopped, and everything removed.

171
00:06:28,068 --> 00:06:32,143
Are both ports free? Count the lines.

172
00:06:32,693 --> 00:06:35,701
Zero. Nothing listens, nothing is left behind.

173
00:06:37,251 --> 00:06:40,536
Your task. Route traffic to a backend with engine X.

174
00:06:41,086 --> 00:06:41,897
One: lab up.

175
00:06:41,897 --> 00:06:44,939
Engine X and the backend are already running.

176
00:06:44,939 --> 00:06:45,818
Curl the API,

177
00:06:45,818 --> 00:06:47,508
and see the four oh four.

178
00:06:48,058 --> 00:06:49,797
Two: in the location block,

179
00:06:49,797 --> 00:06:50,763
add proxy pass,

180
00:06:50,763 --> 00:06:52,179
with a trailing slash.

181
00:06:52,179 --> 00:06:52,501
Test,

182
00:06:52,501 --> 00:06:53,210
and reload.

183
00:06:53,210 --> 00:06:54,884
The backend should answer.

184
00:06:55,434 --> 00:07:00,426
Three: add proxy set header Host, so the backend sees the name the customer used.

185
00:07:00,976 --> 00:07:05,243
Four: add X real I P, X forwarded for, and X forwarded proto.

186
00:07:05,793 --> 00:07:09,078
Five: test, reload, and lab check. Then lab down.

